  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 207 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOverall, confidence in the forecast remains relatively high\nthrough Monday, with confidence rapidly decreasing Tuesday and\nWednesday. This means above normal temperatures and below normal\nprecipitation are forecast through the weekend. \n\nOn Friday, a closed low over southern California will be quasi-\nstationary with a mid-level ridge over the central United\nStates. Sunday into Monday, a potent mid-level wave will move\neast across British Columbia. The latest run of the WPC ESA\nwebpage shows this to be the source of the uncertainty Tuesday \nand Wednesday. Two clusters show a stronger wave that wave \nbreaks (forming a closed off low), while other guidance has a \nmore progressive wave. The wave breaking scenario is favored by \nthe CMC (GEPS), while the ECMWF (EPS) and GFS (GEFS) show a \ncolder solution. When looking at box and whisker plots, the \nLREF and NBM have a 10 to 20 degree spread for Tuesday and \nWednesday. The sensitivity analysis also shows that model \nguidance will likely not find agreement until Sunday. Either \nsolution set shows the area dry through Tuesday, the main \ndifference being temperatures. As of current, it appears ~50% \nsplit between warmer and cooler solutions. Through Monday, \nexpect highs in the upper 70s, with lows around 50 degrees.",
